# Glon Fetch -- application manifest (D7).
#
# The manifest REQUESTS authority; it never grants it. Trusted host-side grant
# state (desktop/grants.conf) is the only source of authority. Effective
# authority = host implements INTERSECT manifest requests INTERSECT grants.
#
# modules      -> functionality (loaded from the local module store, modules/)
# permissions  -> authority
# entitlements -> licensing (present, intentionally empty for D7)
# package      -> identity
#
# Glon Fetch does NOT request process/spawn. Downloading is a BROKERED host
# service: the application asks for a logical fetch; the trusted host service
# implements it (internally with curl) and never exposes arbitrary child-process
# authority to the application. SHA-256 is likewise a host service.

name: Glon Fetch
version: 0.1.0
entry: app.glon
view: view.glon

module: strings
module: fetch

permission: net/connect
permission: file/app-write
permission: open/folder

# entitlements: (none for D7)
